  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated humanitarian response in Mali</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Norwegian Church Aid Malis WASH programme will improve hygiene, sanitation, and water access in targeted communities to safeguard public and personal health. The project ensures inclusive and accessible WASH services by designing water and sanitation facilities that accommodate persons with disabilities and by prioritising the specific hygiene needs of women and girls, including MHM in schools and clinics. Women also play active roles in water-management committees, strengthening gender equality and inclusive decision-making. The response will be implemented together with two national partners: The Malian Association for Survival in the Sahel (AMSS) and Appui pour la Scolarisation et le D&#xe9;veloppement des Enfants pour une Meilleure Int&#xe9;gration Nationale (ASDEMIN)</narrative>
  </description>
